<title>JAPAN: Japan govt to review public spending plan - paper.</title>
<headline>Japan govt to review public spending plan - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government and the ruling Liberal Democratic Party plan to review a 630-trillion-yen public-works spending programme covering a 10-year period to March 2005, a newspaper reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The financial daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said they would seek to extend the 10-year period by two years, which would reduce spending on an annual basis.</p>
